00:28:39.927 --> 00:28:41.178
Yes, Mr President?

474
00:28:41.220 --> 00:28:44.223
Yeah, can you wrangle me up
some Ding Dongs, darling?

475
00:28:56.318 --> 00:29:00.405
I joined the Air Force to bring the man
Ding Dongs. I'll be in storage.

476
00:29:25.764 --> 00:29:26.765
Shoot.

477
00:29:40.904 --> 00:29:42.447
Gross.

478
00:30:09.641 --> 00:30:11.310
Do you hear that?

479
00:30:14.271 --> 00:30:15.856
Are you getting this?

480
00:30:16.815 --> 00:30:18.483
I think they're hacking
the network again.

481
00:30:33.665 --> 00:30:36.835
Oh, my God. This is a direct match
to the signal in Qatar.

482
00:30:36.918 --> 00:30:38.795
-Are you running a diagnostic?
-Should I be?

483
00:30:38.837 --> 00:30:40.881
-Yes, you should.
-So I am.

484
00:30:52.017 --> 00:30:54.311
Someone!
They're hacking into Air Force One!

485
00:30:54.353 --> 00:30:55.937
We need a senior analyst.

486
00:30:56.021 --> 00:30:57.898
- I think they're planting a virus.
-A virus?

487
00:30:57.981 --> 00:31:00.525
-It's streaming right now.
-They are planting a virus

488
00:31:00.609 --> 00:31:03.862
and stealing a whole lot of data
from your system at the same time.

489
00:31:03.904 --> 00:31:05.489
Code Red. We have a breach.

490
00:31:05.530 --> 00:31:08.325
Air Force One, someone onboard
has breached the military network.

491
00:31:08.367 --> 00:31:11.203
I'm in the cargo hold. Clear. Clear.

492
00:31:15.749 --> 00:31:17.209
-You got to cut the hard lines.
-What?

493
00:31:17.250 --> 00:31:20.420
-Whatever they want, they are getting it.
-Sir?

494
00:31:20.504 --> 00:31:23.215
Permission to take down
the Defence Network.

495
00:31:23.298 --> 00:31:27.344
-Cut all server hard lines now.
-Cut all server hard lines now.

496
00:31:48.949 --> 00:31:51.743
Someone's tampered
with the POTUS mainframe.

497
00:31:51.868 --> 00:31:53.328
What the...

498
00:31:58.750 --> 00:32:01.211
Shots fired in the under deck.
Repeat, shots fired.

499
00:32:01.253 --> 00:32:04.131
Crew, prepare for emergency descent.

500
00:32:22.190 --> 00:32:24.234
I want our President in that bunker.

501
00:32:24.276 --> 00:32:28.363
And I don't want to discuss a damn
thing other till that becomes reality.

502
00:32:28.447 --> 00:32:31.575
That's our first priority.
That's our only priority right now.

503
00:32:31.616 --> 00:32:32.784
Air Force One is on the ground.

504
00:33:36.848 --> 00:33:39.518
Oh, God. No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

505
00:33:40.352 --> 00:33:41.937
That's my car!

506
00:33:43.355 --> 00:33:44.689
No!

507
00:33:46.816 --> 00:33:47.943
No, no, no, no.

508
00:33:55.450 --> 00:33:57.577
Dad, call the cops!

509
00:33:59.329 --> 00:34:02.499
Where you going with my car, buddy?
Where you going?

510
00:34:02.541 --> 00:34:06.336
Hello? 911 emergency!
My car has been stolen!

511
00:34:06.378 --> 00:34:09.881
I'm in pursuit! Right?
I need all units, the whole squadron.

512
00:34:09.965 --> 00:34:12.801
Bring everyone!
No, don't ask me questions, all right?

513
00:34:12.884 --> 00:34:15.554
My father's the head
of the neighbourhood watch!

514
00:34:48.169 --> 00:34:49.754
Oh, my God.

515
00:35:06.146 --> 00:35:07.606
My name is Sam Witwicky.

516
00:35:07.647 --> 00:35:11.610
Whoever finds this, my car is alive,
okay? You saw that?

517
00:35:11.693 --> 00:35:14.446
Since this is my last words on Earth,
I just wanna say, Mom, Dad, I love you,

518
00:35:14.529 --> 00:35:16.948
and if you find Busty Beauties
under my bed, it wasn't mine.

519
00:35:16.990 --> 00:35:19.034
I'm holding it for Miles.
No, no, wait that...

520
00:35:19.117 --> 00:35:21.786
Okay, that's not true. It's mine
and Uncle Charles gave it to me.

521
00:35:21.828 --> 00:35:23.830
I'm sorry. Mojo, I love you.

522
00:35:35.467 --> 00:35:37.636
No! No! No! No!

523
00:35:41.139 --> 00:35:42.557
Oh, my God.

524
00:35:43.099 --> 00:35:45.644
No, you're a good dog!
Good dog! Good dog!

525
00:35:45.810 --> 00:35:46.978
Oh, my God.

526
00:35:50.231 --> 00:35:54.986
Whoa! Hey, hey, hey! All right! Oh!
No! No!

527
00:35:57.822 --> 00:35:59.240
Okay. Please, please don't kill me!

528
00:35:59.324 --> 00:36:02.661
I'm sorry! Take the keys!
I don't want them! Car's yours!

529
00:36:04.454 --> 00:36:06.915
Listen, listen, listen.

530
00:36:06.998 --> 00:36:08.333
-Good, you're here.
-Let me see your hands!

531
00:36:08.416 --> 00:36:10.001
-No, no, no! It's not me!
-Let me see your hands.

532
00:36:10.085 --> 00:36:13.171
-The guy's inside.
-Shut up! Walk towards the car.

533
00:36:15.090 --> 00:36:16.841
Put your head on the hood.

534
00:36:30.105 --> 00:36:32.857
Whoever did this finally managed
to infiltrate our defence network,

535
00:36:32.941 --> 00:36:35.527
which is what they tried to do in Qatar,
only this time it worked.

536
00:36:35.568 --> 00:36:37.237
-What did they get?
-We still don't know.

537
00:36:37.320 --> 00:36:40.490
-Talk to me about the virus.
-It's a Spider-bot virus.

538
00:36:40.532 --> 00:36:43.201
We're not sure what it's going to do,
but it may cripple the system.

539
00:36:43.284 --> 00:36:45.328
-Can we stop it?
-Every time we try an anti virus,

540
00:36:45.370 --> 00:36:47.956
it adapts and speeds up.
It's like it's not a virus any more.

541
00:36:48.039 --> 00:36:49.124
It's become the system.

542
00:36:49.207 --> 00:36:52.377
Obviously the first phase
of a major attack against the US.

543
00:36:52.460 --> 00:36:54.087
The only countries
with this kind of capability

544
00:36:54.170 --> 00:36:56.506
are Russia, North Korea, maybe China.

545
00:36:56.548 --> 00:36:59.551
-I'm sorry, that's not correct.
-Excuse me, young lady.

546
00:36:59.592 --> 00:37:01.886
I didn't see you standing there.
You would be who?

547
00:37:01.928 --> 00:37:03.805
I'm just the analyst
who detected the hack.

548
00:37:03.888 --> 00:37:07.058
Hold on. It was you? You did it?

549
00:37:07.392 --> 00:37:10.186
-Her team.
-Sir, I was just trying to say,

550
00:37:10.228 --> 00:37:12.897
they hacked your firewall in 10 seconds.

551
00:37:12.981 --> 00:37:15.692
Okay. Even a supercomputer
with a brute force attack

552
00:37:15.734 --> 00:37:17.527
would take 20 years to do that.

553
00:37:17.569 --> 00:37:20.071
Maybe you can explain, then,
how our latest satellite imagery

554
00:37:20.155 --> 00:37:22.532
shows North Korea
doubling its naval activity.

555
00:37:22.574 --> 00:37:26.119
Maybe it's a precaution,
because isn't that what we're doing?

556
00:37:26.202 --> 00:37:29.581
The signal pattern is learning.
It's evolving on its own.

557
00:37:29.664 --> 00:37:31.958
And you need to
move past Fourier transfers

558
00:37:32.041 --> 00:37:34.252
and start considering
quantum mechanics.

559
00:37:34.335 --> 00:37:36.713
There is nothing on Earth that complex.

560
00:37:36.755 --> 00:37:39.299
What about an organism?
A living organism?

561
00:37:39.382 --> 00:37:41.801
Maybe some kind of
DNA-based computer?

562
00:37:41.885 --> 00:37:45.597
-And I know that that sounds crazy...
-That's enough. That's enough.

563
00:37:46.014 --> 00:37:48.600
We have six floors of analysts
working on this thing.

564
00:37:48.683 --> 00:37:51.060
Now, if you can find proof to back up
your theory,

565
00:37:51.102 --> 00:37:53.646
I'm gonna be happy to listen to you.
But if you don't get a filter

566
00:37:53.730 --> 00:37:57.692
on that brain-mouth thing, you're gonna
be off the team. You understand?

567
00:38:03.114 --> 00:38:06.618
Look, I can't be any clearer
than how crystal clear I am being.

568
00:38:07.452 --> 00:38:09.871
-It just stood up.
-It just stood up.

569
00:38:11.331 --> 00:38:13.124
Wow. That's really neat.

570
00:38:14.083 --> 00:38:15.335
Okay, chiefie.

571
00:38:15.710 --> 00:38:18.505
Time to fill her up. And no drippy-drippy.

572
00:38:19.005 --> 00:38:20.423
What are you rolling?

573
00:38:20.465 --> 00:38:22.842
Whippets? Goofballs?
A little wowie sauce with the boys?

574
00:38:22.926 --> 00:38:25.303
-No, I'm not on any drugs.
-What's these?

575
00:38:26.095 --> 00:38:28.932
Found it in your pocket. "Mojo."

576
00:38:30.141 --> 00:38:32.811
Is that what the kids are doing now?
Little bit of Mojo?

577
00:38:32.852 --> 00:38:36.523
-Those are my dog's pain pills.
-You know, a Chihuahua. A little...

578
00:38:40.485 --> 00:38:41.778
What was that?

579
00:38:43.404 --> 00:38:46.616
You eyeballing my piece, 50 Cent?

580
00:38:47.742 --> 00:38:51.246
You wanna go?
Make something happen. Do it.

581
00:38:51.329 --> 00:38:54.541
"Cause I promise you I will bust you up.

582
00:38:55.750 --> 00:38:57.043
Are you on drugs?

583
00:39:05.718 --> 00:39:08.012
Let's hope this telephone line works.

584
00:39:10.515 --> 00:39:13.017
Hey, heads up!

585
00:39:13.059 --> 00:39:16.729
Heads up! Hey! Heads up!

586
00:39:21.651 --> 00:39:23.653
What the heck was that?

587
00:39:28.283 --> 00:39:30.660
English, dude. English.

588
00:39:37.041 --> 00:39:38.209
Whoa!

589
00:39:38.835 --> 00:39:40.378
Watch out!

590
00:39:46.593 --> 00:39:49.095
-Open fire!
-Contact! Contact!

591
00:39:49.178 --> 00:39:50.263
Everybody, quiet. Settle.

592
00:39:50.346 --> 00:39:52.515
Whoa, mother... What the hell is...

593
00:40:00.231 --> 00:40:03.026
Get up! Get up! Come on!

594
00:40:10.074 --> 00:40:11.910
Go! Move it!

595
00:40:24.172 --> 00:40:26.341
Take cover!

596
00:40:28.676 --> 00:40:30.720
Fig! Cover the rear!

597
00:40:31.304 --> 00:40:36.267
Cover fire! Move it! Fig, cover the rear!
Epps! Cover the rear! Move it!

598
00:40:36.309 --> 00:40:39.395
Come on! Give me a mag!

599
00:40:40.605 --> 00:40:42.231
Where's your papa?
Where's your papa?

600
00:40:42.273 --> 00:40:43.441
Papal

601
00:40:44.025 --> 00:40:46.277
Sir, we need... I need a telephone.

602
00:40:46.361 --> 00:40:48.780
-Telephone, telephone, yes!
-Telephone!

603
00:40:48.821 --> 00:40:50.448
Hey, I need a mag! Give me a mag!

604
00:40:50.531 --> 00:40:51.824
-Cell phone!
- I don't know how to thank you.

605
00:40:51.908 --> 00:40:52.909
Fire!

606
00:40:54.118 --> 00:40:56.704
This is an emergency Pentagon call!
I need you to... Do you understand?

607
00:40:56.788 --> 00:40:59.290
It's an emergency Pentagon...

608
00:41:01.125 --> 00:41:03.294
I don't have a credit card!

609
00:41:03.753 --> 00:41:07.507
Sir, the attitude is not going to speed
things up any bit at all.

610
00:41:07.590 --> 00:41:10.301
I'm going to ask you to speak
into the mouthpiece very clearly.

611
00:41:10.385 --> 00:41:14.722
I'm in the middle of a war!
This is frigging ridiculous!

612
00:41:16.015 --> 00:41:17.350
Ammo!

613
00:41:17.850 --> 00:41:20.103
I need a credit card!

614
00:41:22.021 --> 00:41:24.816
-Epps! Where's your wallet?
-Pocket!

615
00:41:25.483 --> 00:41:28.194
-Which pocket?
-My back pocket!

616
00:41:28.277 --> 00:41:32.490
-You got 10 back pockets!
-Left cheek! Left cheek! Left cheek!

617
00:41:33.324 --> 00:41:35.493
All right, keep shooting! Keep shooting!

618
00:41:35.576 --> 00:41:37.620
Okay, it's Visa.

619
00:41:37.829 --> 00:41:39.122
Also, sir, have you heard about

620
00:41:39.163 --> 00:41:41.332
our premium plus
world-service gold package?

621
00:41:41.374 --> 00:41:46.546
No, I don't want a premium package!
Epps! Pentagon!

622
00:41:49.507 --> 00:41:50.842
Give me a status.

623
00:41:51.175 --> 00:41:53.803
Sir, we're tracking a Special Ops team
under fire in Qatar.

624
00:41:53.845 --> 00:41:55.596
They say they're survivors
of the base attack.

625
00:41:55.680 --> 00:41:56.681
Survivors?

626
00:42:00.476 --> 00:42:02.186
I ain't never seen this in my life!

627
00:42:02.228 --> 00:42:04.022
Need gunships on station ASAP!

628
00:42:04.063 --> 00:42:05.314
Predator's coming up in a minute.

629
00:42:05.356 --> 00:42:06.816
We're linking the call
to the nearest AWACS.

630
00:42:13.031 --> 00:42:16.034
Unknown, man. I don't...
Man, if you seen this shit...

631
00:42:16.367 --> 00:42:19.037
Predator ETA two minutes.

632
00:42:27.754 --> 00:42:29.714
Hey! Make way!

633
00:42:34.552 --> 00:42:36.679
-What is that?
-I don't know.

634
00:42:41.893 --> 00:42:43.644
We need air support
and we need it now.

635
00:42:43.728 --> 00:42:46.856
Roll in strike package Bravo
on unknown target.

636
00:42:46.898 --> 00:42:50.568
I authenticate Tango Whiskey
at time 0300 Zulu.

637
00:42:50.610 --> 00:42:53.488
Attention, all aircraft. This will be
a danger close-fire mission.

638
00:42:53.571 --> 00:42:55.114
Weapons, I just got a call
from Falcon Ops.

639
00:42:55.198 --> 00:42:56.908
Who's closer to Kill Box One Alpha?

640
00:42:56.991 --> 00:42:58.576
-Send the Hogs, sir.
-Okay, send the Hogs over

641
00:42:58.618 --> 00:43:00.369
to Kill Box One Alpha.
It's a danger close...

642
00:43:00.411 --> 00:43:02.997
Switch the Hogs to Kill Box One Alpha,
300 feet danger close.

643
00:43:03.081 --> 00:43:04.999
Friendlies in the area.

644
00:43:05.083 --> 00:43:08.127
Seven-man team
north of orange smoke!

645
00:43:08.211 --> 00:43:11.464
Received Kill Box One Alpha.
Engage hostile.

646
00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:17.095
Attack direction west!
You're clear and hot!

647
00:43:20.264 --> 00:43:21.682
Strike, tell me status of Hog right now.

648
00:43:21.766 --> 00:43:23.643
Hog One-One Dark Star status.

649
00:43:25.978 --> 00:43:29.107
-Lennox! The heat's coming!
-Laze the target!

650
00:43:29.190 --> 00:43:31.776
We got a beam-rider incoming!
Laze target!

651
00:43:39.117 --> 00:43:41.786
-Ready! Heat's coming!
-What? Bring it!

652
00:43:41.828 --> 00:43:44.455
Receiving radar jamming
in vicinity of target.

653
00:44:00.805 --> 00:44:02.640
No frigging way
that thing's still not down.

654
00:44:02.682 --> 00:44:05.977
Spooky Three Two, use 105 shells.
Bring the rain.

655
00:44:08.146 --> 00:44:11.649
Be advised, ground team is requesting
105 sabot rounds.

656
00:44:39.844 --> 00:44:40.970
Did we lose them?

657
00:44:41.012 --> 00:44:43.639
Warthog One confirm visual
on friendlies.

658
00:44:47.685 --> 00:44:48.853
Where's Fig?

659
00:44:49.770 --> 00:44:51.397
-Fig? Fig?
-Oh, God!

660
00:44:52.356 --> 00:44:54.192
-God damn it!
-Get a medic!

661
00:44:54.233 --> 00:44:55.359
Get a medic!

662
00:44:55.526 --> 00:44:56.569
-I'm sorry.
-Black Hawk...

663
00:44:56.652 --> 00:44:57.862
We'll get a medic. Just hold on.
He's got a pulse.

664
00:44:57.945 --> 00:44:59.864
We need a medevac. One man down.
Patient care category urgent.

665
00:45:05.536 --> 00:45:07.288
Bring them home.

666
00:45:08.664 --> 00:45:11.042
You get those men stateside right now.

667
00:45:11.375 --> 00:45:13.085
I want them debriefed in 10 hours.

668
00:45:19.967 --> 00:45:23.387
There's only one hacker in the world
who can break this code.

669
00:45:33.814 --> 00:45:36.567
Hey! Hey, hey, hey! Wait! Stop!

670
00:45:39.612 --> 00:45:41.364
I am sorry to bother you.

671
00:45:41.614 --> 00:45:43.282
-Maggie?
-Listen, I need your help.

672
00:45:43.366 --> 00:45:47.411
No! This is my private area,
my place of Zen and peace.

673
00:45:47.453 --> 00:45:49.163
-Listen to me.
-Glen! Who is it?

674
00:45:49.247 --> 00:45:51.415
Shut up, Grandma!

675
00:45:51.457 --> 00:45:53.918
-What are you doing here?
-Just give me a break, will you, please?

676
00:45:54.001 --> 00:45:56.128
Grandmamal! Drink your prune juice!

677
00:46:01.092 --> 00:46:03.636
-What level are you on, man?
-Six.

678
00:46:06.430 --> 00:46:09.141
Oh, here come the matrix!
Here come the matrix!

679
00:46:12.728 --> 00:46:15.606
Glen, seriously, don't you
want to see something classified?

680
00:46:15.648 --> 00:46:17.525
Yeah. Get low.

681
00:46:17.817 --> 00:46:21.779
-Here we go. Here we go. Double tap.
-Hey, I just paused it. I just paused it.

682
00:46:21.862 --> 00:46:23.739
Hey. I need a moment.

683
00:46:24.699 --> 00:46:26.075
-Please.
-Sorry.

684
00:46:26.617 --> 00:46:28.244
Hey, man, save my game.

685
00:46:28.286 --> 00:46:30.204
How classified?

686
00:46:31.497 --> 00:46:35.626
Like "I will go to jail for the rest of
my life for showing you" classified.

687
00:46:35.835 --> 00:46:37.837
Yes! One quick peek.

688
00:46:38.629 --> 00:46:41.799
Special Ops got a thermal snapshot
of whatever hit the base in Qatar.

689
00:46:41.882 --> 00:46:44.468
-I want to see it.
-Well, the imager was damaged, sir.

690
00:46:44.510 --> 00:46:46.137
The rangers are en route
with the imager,

691
00:46:46.178 --> 00:46:48.139
but we also have a security issue.

692
00:46:48.180 --> 00:46:50.474
Circle logs indicate one of
the analysts made a copy

693
00:46:50.558 --> 00:46:52.268
of the network intrusion signal.

694
00:46:55.229 --> 00:46:58.566
The signal strength is through the roof.
Where did you say you got this?

695
00:46:58.649 --> 00:47:00.985
It hacked the national military
air-guard frequency

696
00:47:01.068 --> 00:47:02.653
in less than a minute.

697
00:47:02.737 --> 00:47:04.989
-No way.
-Yeah.

698
00:47:06.407 --> 00:47:10.870
Looks like there's a message embedded
in the signal. Let me work my magic.

699
00:47:17.001 --> 00:47:18.586
"Project Iceman"?

700
00:47:18.669 --> 00:47:22.089
-What's Sector Seven?
-Who is Captain Witwicky?

701
00:47:23.591 --> 00:47:25.968
Are you playing
those video games again?

702
00:47:26.135 --> 00:47:28.179
Cops! Cops!

703
00:47:28.220 --> 00:47:30.973
FBI! Clear right!

704
00:47:32.683 --> 00:47:34.894
Lock it down! Lock it down!

705
00:47:36.562 --> 00:47:37.563
Cops!

706
00:47:37.813 --> 00:47:39.023
Lock it down.

707
00:47:39.065 --> 00:47:42.610
Wait! I'm just a cousin! I'm just a...

708
00:47:43.694 --> 00:47:47.281
Get off my Grandmama's carpet!
She don't like nobody on the carpet!

709
00:47:47.365 --> 00:47:49.033
Especially police!

710
00:47:49.575 --> 00:47:52.370
It was an awesome spectacle here
an hour ago

711
00:47:52.453 --> 00:47:56.374
when over 40 C-17s lifted off
of this very base.

712
00:47:56.957 --> 00:47:59.043
We're not told where they're going.

713
00:47:59.085 --> 00:48:00.127
Morning, Mo.

714
00:48:00.211 --> 00:48:02.546
The government has been very quiet
about what's going on but in our...

715
00:48:02.588 --> 00:48:04.256
-Mojo. Mojo.
-They were headed directly

716
00:48:04.340 --> 00:48:05.883
towards North Korea.

717
00:48:05.966 --> 00:48:08.886
Stop with the barking, Mojo.
It's too early. Please?

718
00:48:12.431 --> 00:48:14.225
Miles? Miles, listen to me. Listen.

719
00:48:14.308 --> 00:48:17.395
-My car, it stole itself, okay?
-What are you talking about, man?

720
00:48:17.436 --> 00:48:20.398
Satan's Camaro. In my yard.
It's stalking me.

721
00:48:28.239 --> 00:48:29.281
Stop!

722
00:48:29.365 --> 00:48:31.117
No, no, no, no, no, no.

723
00:48:37.581 --> 00:48:38.749
Oh, my God!

724
00:48:39.583 --> 00:48:40.584
Sam?

725
00:48:43.629 --> 00:48:44.630
Hi.

726
00:48:44.922 --> 00:48:48.217
That was... That was really awesome.

727
00:48:48.259 --> 00:48:50.428
-Well, it felt awesome.
-Are you okay?

728
00:48:50.469 --> 00:48:52.513
I'm not okay, all right?
I'm losing my mind a little bit.

729
00:48:52.596 --> 00:48:54.473
I'm getting chased by my car right now.
I got to go.

730
00:48:54.557 --> 00:48:56.809
You know what?
I'm gonna catch up with you guys later.

731
00:49:29.675 --> 00:49:31.302
Oh, great. Cops.

732
00:49:36.348 --> 00:49:37.600
Officer!

733
00:49:39.185 --> 00:49:40.978
Listen!

734
00:49:42.480 --> 00:49:43.481
Oh, that hurt.

735
00:49:46.192 --> 00:49:47.735
Listen to me!

736
00:49:47.818 --> 00:49:50.696
Thank God you're here!
I've had the worst day ever!

737
00:49:50.779 --> 00:49:54.492
I've been... I've been followed here
on my mother's bike! Right?

738
00:49:54.533 --> 00:49:57.161
And my car's right there
and it's been following me here!

739
00:49:57.244 --> 00:50:03.751
So get out of the car! No! Stop!
Oh, God. Okay, okay! Okay, all right!

740
00:50:04.043 --> 00:50:08.547
Okay! I'm sorry! I'm...
I didn't mean to hit your car! Look!

741
00:50:09.840 --> 00:50:13.719
Okay, look, look, look! Stop, stop!

742
00:50:17.848 --> 00:50:20.684
Please! Okay,
what do you want from me?

743
00:50:22.978 --> 00:50:24.396
Okay.

744
00:50:29.902 --> 00:50:31.403
Oh, God, no! No!

745
00:50:33.322 --> 00:50:38.786
Oh, shit! Oh, shit, shit, shit!
Oh, God! Oh, shit!

746
00:50:41.789 --> 00:50:43.582
It's a bad dream.

747
00:50:45.417 --> 00:50:47.211
Are you username LadiesMan217?

748
00:50:47.294 --> 00:50:48.504
I don't know what you're talking about!

749
00:50:48.546 --> 00:50:50.965
Are you username LadiesMan217?

750
00:50:51.048 --> 00:50:52.216
Yeah.

751
00:50:52.258 --> 00:50:54.718
Where is eBay item 211537

752
00:50:54.802 --> 00:50:56.554
Where are the glasses?

753
00:51:08.065 --> 00:51:09.400
Get back!

754
00:51:10.234 --> 00:51:11.235
Stop!

755
00:51:14.363 --> 00:51:15.364
God!

756
00:51:16.240 --> 00:51:18.033
What is your problem, Sam?

757
00:51:18.075 --> 00:51:20.119
Okay, there's a monster right there!
It just attacked me!

758
00:51:20.202 --> 00:51:24.665
Here he comes! All right, get up.
Get up and run! You have to run! Okay.

759
00:51:32.298 --> 00:51:33.382
Sam, what is that thing?

760
00:51:33.424 --> 00:51:34.842
-You have to get in the car. Get in.
- I don't want to.

761
00:51:34.925 --> 00:51:37.052
-Get in the car. Trust me. Trust me!
-Sam.

762
00:51:37.094 --> 00:51:41.515
Get in! Go, go, go, go, go.

763
00:51:53.110 --> 00:51:54.445
Go, go, go, go!

764
00:51:59.033 --> 00:52:00.868
Oh, God! We're gonna die!
We're gonna die!

765
00:52:00.951 --> 00:52:02.536
No, we're not. No, we're not gonna die.

766
00:52:02.620 --> 00:52:04.955
-Oh, my God!
-Trust me. He's a kick-ass driver!

767
00:52:05.539 --> 00:52:06.957
Oh, my God! No!

768
00:52:07.041 --> 00:52:08.375
We're gonna die!

769
00:52:14.381 --> 00:52:15.799
Oh, my God!

770
00:52:33.150 --> 00:52:34.318
We're locked in.

771
00:52:36.820 --> 00:52:40.282
The car won't start.
At least we ditched the monster, right?

772
00:52:46.163 --> 00:52:47.289
Okay.

773
00:52:48.832 --> 00:52:50.334
Time to start.

774
00:53:54.648 --> 00:53:55.983
He's got me! Oh, God!

775
00:54:02.489 --> 00:54:04.408
He's going to kill me!

776
00:54:07.494 --> 00:54:09.204
No. No, no, no!

777
00:54:23.761 --> 00:54:24.970
Get off!

778
00:54:39.610 --> 00:54:40.652
Kill it! Kill it!

779
00:54:40.736 --> 00:54:42.321
Get it, get it, get it, get it!

780
00:54:49.119 --> 00:54:51.121
Not so tough without a head, are you?

781
00:54:57.044 --> 00:54:58.504
Here, come on.

782
00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:14.812
What is it?

783
00:55:16.188 --> 00:55:17.648
It's a robot.

784
00:55:19.024 --> 00:55:20.359
But like a...

785
00:55:20.484 --> 00:55:23.987
Like a different...
You know, like a super-advanced robot.

786
00:55:25.322 --> 00:55:26.824
It's probably Japanese.

787
00:55:26.865 --> 00:55:29.326
Yeah, it's definitely Japanese.

788
00:55:30.869 --> 00:55:32.621
What are you doing?

789
00:55:33.205 --> 00:55:36.416
I don't think it wants to hurt us.
It would have done that already.

790
00:55:36.500 --> 00:55:38.836
Really? Well, do you speak robot?

791
00:55:38.877 --> 00:55:42.339
Because they just had, like,
a giant droid death match.

792
00:55:43.674 --> 00:55:46.844
- I think it wants something from me.
-What?

793
00:55:46.927 --> 00:55:49.471
Well, 'cause the other one was
talking about my eBay page.

794
00:55:50.305 --> 00:55:53.100
You are the strangest boy
I have ever met.

795
00:55:53.559 --> 00:55:55.769
-Can you talk?
-XM Satellite Radio...

796
00:55:55.853 --> 00:55:59.439
Digital cable brings you...
...Columbia Broadcasting System...

797
00:55:59.523 --> 00:56:01.316
So you... You talk through the radio?

798
00:56:01.358 --> 00:56:04.319
Thank you, you're beautiful.
You're wonderful, you're wonderful.

799
00:56:04.361 --> 00:56:06.405
So, what was that last night?
What was that?

800
00:56:06.488 --> 00:56:07.990
Message from Starfleet, Captain...

801
00:56:08.031 --> 00:56:10.158
Throughout the inanimate vastness
of space...

802
00:56:10.200 --> 00:56:12.202
Angels will rain down
like visitors from heaven! Hallelujah!

803
00:56:12.286 --> 00:56:14.454
Visitors from heaven? What...

804
00:56:14.538 --> 00:56:16.707
What are you,
like, an alien or something?

805
00:56:22.462 --> 00:56:25.007
Any more questions you want to ask?

806
00:56:25.632 --> 00:56:27.843
He wants us to get in the car.

807
00:56:28.844 --> 00:56:30.345
And go where?

808
00:56:31.305 --> 00:56:33.098
Fifty years from now,
when you're looking back at your life,

809
00:56:33.223 --> 00:56:36.310
don't you want to be able to say
you had the guts to get in the car?

810
00:57:05.756 --> 00:57:07.507
This car's a pretty good driver.

811
00:57:07.591 --> 00:57:08.759
I know.

812
00:57:11.428 --> 00:57:13.430
Why don't you go sit in that seat, there?

813
00:57:13.513 --> 00:57:15.724
I'm not going to sit in that seat.
He's driving.

814
00:57:15.766 --> 00:57:16.892
Yeah.

815
00:57:18.268 --> 00:57:19.770
You're right.

816
00:57:21.271 --> 00:57:24.274
-Well, maybe you should sit in my lap.
-Why?

817
00:57:25.442 --> 00:57:29.237
Well, I have the only seat belt here.
You know, safety first.

818
00:57:31.281 --> 00:57:32.699
-Yeah, all right.
-Right?

819
00:57:32.783 --> 00:57:34.368
-Yeah.
-Okay.

820
00:57:36.787 --> 00:57:38.830
There, see? That's better.

821
00:57:39.122 --> 00:57:40.540
-Okay.
-Okay.

822
00:57:44.211 --> 00:57:47.631
You know, that seat belt thing was
a pretty smooth move.

823
00:57:48.632 --> 00:57:49.633
Thank you.

824
00:57:50.676 --> 00:57:52.844
You know what I don't understand?

825
00:57:52.928 --> 00:57:56.014
Why, if he's supposed to be, like,
this super-advanced robot,

826
00:57:56.098 --> 00:57:58.725
does he transform back
into this piece-of-crap Camaro?

827
00:58:00.143 --> 00:58:01.478
Whoa! Whoa!

828
00:58:01.520 --> 00:58:04.314
Oh, see? No. Get...
No, that doesn't work. See?

829
00:58:04.398 --> 00:58:05.482
Move it, you moron!

830
00:58:05.565 --> 00:58:07.651
Great, now... See?

831
00:58:08.986 --> 00:58:10.153
Fantastic.

832
00:58:10.237 --> 00:58:12.155
Now you pissed him off.

833
00:58:12.406 --> 00:58:13.907
That car is sensitive.

834
00:58:13.991 --> 00:58:16.201
I mean, $4000 just drove off.

835
00:58:29.339 --> 00:58:30.465
What?

836
00:59:34.196 --> 00:59:35.572
This is you...

837
00:59:40.702 --> 00:59:42.621
Oh, my God!

838
00:59:49.836 --> 00:59:51.588
Come on, let's go.

839
00:59:56.426 --> 00:59:59.679
This is the coolest thing I've ever seen!
Explosions everywhere!

840
00:59:59.763 --> 01:00:03.266
This is easily a hundred times cooler
than Armageddon. I swear to God!

841
01:00:03.350 --> 01:00:05.602
Fire, fire, fire, fire!

842
01:00:19.533 --> 01:00:21.201
Whoa! Sweet!

843
01:00:21.284 --> 01:00:23.453
Oh, dude, I hope this guy's got
asteroid insurance,

844
01:00:23.495 --> 01:00:24.788
"cause he is so boned!

845
01:00:28.667 --> 01:00:30.043
What is that?

846
01:00:30.544 --> 01:00:32.170
There's something in the tree, dude.

847
01:00:32.254 --> 01:00:34.422
No, there's something
in the thing by the tree!

848
01:00:34.464 --> 01:00:35.841
Could you guys just give me
a space rock?

849
01:01:11.209 --> 01:01:13.753
Excuse me, are you the tooth fairy?

850
01:01:15.005 --> 01:01:18.341
Hey, sweetheart, what are you doing
out here by yourself?

851
01:01:18.425 --> 01:01:20.969
Holy God! What happened to the pool?

852
01:02:53.436 --> 01:02:57.691
Are you Samuel James Witwicky,
descendent of Archibald Witwicky?

853
01:02:58.817 --> 01:03:00.610
They know your name.

854
01:03:01.528 --> 01:03:02.529
Yeah.

855
01:03:02.612 --> 01:03:05.073
My name is Optimus Prime.

856
01:03:05.115 --> 01:03:09.244
We are autonomous robotic organisms
from the planet Cybertron.

857
01:03:09.286 --> 01:03:12.706
-But you can call us Autobots for short.
-Autobots.

858
01:03:12.872 --> 01:03:18.169
-What's cracking, little bitches?
-My first lieutenant. Designation, Jazz.

859
01:03:18.253 --> 01:03:21.798
This looks like a cool place to kick it.

860
01:03:22.340 --> 01:03:24.259
What is that?
How did he learn to talk like that?

861
01:03:24.301 --> 01:03:27.971
We've learned Earth's languages
through the World Wide Web.

862
01:03:29.431 --> 01:03:31.933
My weapons specialist, Ironhide.

863
01:03:32.809 --> 01:03:36.396
-You feeling lucky, punk?
-Easy, Ironhide.

864
01:03:36.479 --> 01:03:39.733
Just kidding.
I just wanted to show him my cannons.

865
01:03:40.942 --> 01:03:43.153
Our medical officer, Ratchet.

866
01:03:43.194 --> 01:03:47.365
The boy's pheromone level suggests
he wants to mate with the female.

867
01:03:49.743 --> 01:03:53.121
You already know
your guardian, Bumblebee.

868
01:03:53.330 --> 01:03:54.998
Bumblebee, right?

869
01:03:55.081 --> 01:03:56.833
Check on the rep
Yep, second to none

870
01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:59.294
So you're my guardian, huh?

871
01:03:59.336 --> 01:04:04.591
His vocal processors were damaged
in battle. I'm still working on them.

872
01:04:09.387 --> 01:04:10.805
Why are you here?

873
01:04:10.847 --> 01:04:16.144
We are here looking for the All Spark.
And we must find it before Megatron.

874
01:04:16.436 --> 01:04:17.896
Mega-what?

875
01:04:27.447 --> 01:04:33.078
Our planet was once a powerful empire,
peaceful and just,

876
01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:39.000
until we were betrayed by Megatron,
leader of the Decepticons.

877
01:04:40.043 --> 01:04:43.380
All who defied them were destroyed.

878
01:04:43.421 --> 01:04:49.552
Our war finally consumed the planet,
and the All Spark was lost to the stars.

879
01:04:50.512 --> 01:04:56.559
Megatron followed it to Earth,
where Captain Witwicky found him.

880
01:04:57.685 --> 01:04:59.396
My grandfather.

881
01:04:59.479 --> 01:05:03.733
It was an accident
that intertwined our fates.

882
01:05:06.903 --> 01:05:08.488
Come back!

883
01:05:10.990 --> 01:05:13.576
I think the dogs have found something.

884
01:05:14.619 --> 01:05:16.413
The ice is cracking!

885
01:05:25.755 --> 01:05:28.842
Captain! Grab my rope, Captain!

886
01:05:29.551 --> 01:05:31.594
I'm all right, lads!

887
01:05:32.720 --> 01:05:35.390
Can we throw you a rope, Captain?

888
01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:47.861
Megatron crash-landed
before he could retrieve the Cube.

889
01:05:51.406 --> 01:05:54.909
Men! We've made a discovery!

890
01:05:54.951 --> 01:05:59.414
He accidentally activated
his navigation system.

891
01:06:12.969 --> 01:06:18.808
The coordinates to the Cube's location
on Earth were imprinted on his glasses.

892
01:06:18.892 --> 01:06:20.977
How'd you know about his glasses?

893
01:06:21.019 --> 01:06:23.313
-eBay.
-eBay.

894
01:06:23.354 --> 01:06:26.566
If the Decepticons find the All Spark,

895
01:06:26.649 --> 01:06:32.489
they will use its power to transform
Earth's machines and build a new army.

896
01:06:32.572 --> 01:06:35.992
And the human race
will be extinguished.

897
01:06:36.075 --> 01:06:41.581
Sam Witwicky,
you hold the key to Earth's survival.

898
01:06:44.542 --> 01:06:47.545
Please tell me
that you have those glasses.

899
01:06:51.674 --> 01:06:55.136
It's like
a self-regenerating molecular arm our.

900
01:06:55.178 --> 01:06:57.222
Look at the scorch mark
where the sabot round hit.

901
01:06:57.305 --> 01:06:58.598
Melted right through.

902
01:06:58.681 --> 01:07:01.893
Hey, aren't sabots hot-loaded for, like,
a 6,000-degree magnesium burn?

903
01:07:02.018 --> 01:07:04.229
Close to it. It melts tank arm our.

904
01:07:04.312 --> 01:07:06.523
So this metal skin must react
to extreme heat.

905
01:07:06.856 --> 01:07:08.942
-Heads up!
-Oh!

906
01:07:09.651 --> 01:07:12.362
I thought you said
that thing was dead, man!

907
01:07:12.695 --> 01:07:16.491
Strap it down! Strap it!
This thing is wicked.

908
01:07:16.533 --> 01:07:17.909
All right, get on the horn
with Northern Command.

909
01:07:17.992 --> 01:07:20.286
Tell them that our effective weapon
is high-heat sabot rounds.

910
01:07:20.370 --> 01:07:21.871
Recommend we load them
on all the gunships. Go.

911
01:07:27.043 --> 01:07:28.795
You want that piece?

912
01:07:28.878 --> 01:07:32.215
Okay, Maggie, look. Let me break
it down to you how it's gonna happen.

913
01:07:32.257 --> 01:07:34.384
They gonna come through that door
and be good cop, bad cop.

914
01:07:34.425 --> 01:07:37.804
Don't fall for that, all right?
That's why I ate their food.

915
01:07:37.887 --> 01:07:40.473
See, they put the plate of donuts
out here to test your guilt.

916
01:07:40.557 --> 01:07:43.059
If you don't touch it, you're guilty.

917
01:07:43.101 --> 01:07:46.980
I ate the whole plate.
The whole plate. Okay?

918
01:07:47.063 --> 01:07:48.231
It's me and you.

919
01:07:48.314 --> 01:07:51.192
They walk through that door,
you don't say nothing.

920
01:08:05.206 --> 01:08:08.251
She did it! She did it!
She's the one you want! All right?

921
01:08:08.334 --> 01:08:10.003
I was just sitting at home
watching cartoons,

922
01:08:10.086 --> 01:08:12.088
playing video games with my cousin,
and she came in there.

923
01:08:12.171 --> 01:08:13.172
-And then...
-Glen, you freak.

924
01:08:13.256 --> 01:08:15.508
Hey! I am not going to jail for you
or anybody else!

925
01:08:15.592 --> 01:08:20.305
I have done nothing bad my entire life!
Hey, man, I'm still a virgin.

926
01:08:20.388 --> 01:08:21.389
Okay, so what?

927
01:08:21.431 --> 01:08:23.600
I've downloaded a couple of
thousand songs off the Internet.

928
01:08:23.641 --> 01:08:25.393
Who hasn't? Who hasn't?

929
01:08:25.435 --> 01:08:26.436
- I promise!
-Glen, shut up!

930
01:08:26.519 --> 01:08:30.398
No, you shut up! Don't talk to me!
Don't talk to me, criminal!

931
01:08:32.650 --> 01:08:34.777
-Oh, sugar rush.
-This is... This is not his fault.

932
01:08:34.861 --> 01:08:36.487
See? So can I go home now?

933
01:08:36.571 --> 01:08:38.823
-Oh, okay. I won't.
-But just listen to me.

934
01:08:38.906 --> 01:08:42.619
Okay, whoever hacked into your military
system downloaded a file, all right?

935
01:08:42.702 --> 01:08:45.079
It was something about
someone named Witwicky

936
01:08:45.121 --> 01:08:48.791
and some government group, right?
Named Sector Seven.

937
01:08:48.833 --> 01:08:50.627
You have to let me talk to
Defence Secretary Keller

938
01:08:50.668 --> 01:08:53.004
before you go to war
with the wrong country!

939
01:08:53.087 --> 01:08:55.965
Whatever fell out of the sky
ended up right behind...

940
01:08:56.007 --> 01:08:57.634
-What did he say?
-What?

941
01:08:57.717 --> 01:08:59.218
-Did he hear it, too?
-Yeah, Jack heard it, too. Yeah.

942
01:08:59.302 --> 01:09:01.888
-What does he think it is?
-He thinks it's a military experiment.

943
01:09:01.971 --> 01:09:03.389
-What a knucklehead.
-Yeah, well, I think it's a plane.

944
01:09:08.728 --> 01:09:10.605
Still no official word as to
what happened. You can see...

945
01:09:10.647 --> 01:09:11.898
-Yeah!
-Call Sam.

946
01:09:11.981 --> 01:09:13.566
-Yeah. Why?
-He should be home in 15 minutes.

947
01:09:13.650 --> 01:09:14.984
Well, I'll call him in 15 minutes.

948
01:09:15.026 --> 01:09:17.612
If you wait 15 minutes, he'll be late
and you'll have to ground him.

949
01:09:17.654 --> 01:09:19.322
Well, I can't ground him
if he's not late, can I?

950
01:09:24.577 --> 01:09:26.037
I need you to stay here, all right?

951
01:09:26.120 --> 01:09:27.330
You got to stay here
and you're gonna watch them.

952
